    "body": "> Greetings!\r\n> \r\n> Please try the following:\r\n> \r\n> 1. Use BepInEx's own `Logger` instance instead of Unity's. For example, instead of `UnityEngine.Debug.Log` you can use `Logger.LogInfo`. `Logger` is a property provided by `BaseUnityPlugin`.\r\n> 2. You can try setting `HideManagerGameObject = true` in BepInEx.cfg. If you don't have that option in the config, update your BepInEx version\r\n> \r\n> The first step is to rule out `Debug.Log` not being logged (this can happen in some games). The second option is to test that the MonoBehaviour is really being destroyed. The second case is extremely rare, so it's better first to test logging.\r\n\r\nchanging the HideManagerGameObject works fine, thank you",
